---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The One-Path Error: The Economics of Autonomous Coding"
  description="About: The One-Path Error: The Economics of Autonomous Coding. Economics essay in the OpenIE research catalog."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Economics essay · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      The One-Path Error: The Economics of Autonomous Coding
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The economics companion to the Reality Code Engine (RCE) research paper. The race to own the projected trillion-dollar AI coding industry assumes there is only one path to autonomous computer automation: high energy, high compute, high entropy and disorder. On that path every task pays for generation again.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      The essay argues that the one-path assumption is an economic error. A second path retrieves and proves code that already exists and pays a model once per new case, so the marginal cost of a covered task falls toward the energy to run it. Price per call and calls per task are two declines that multiply.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-gray leading-relaxed">
      The trillion-dollar figure is a cited value estimate, not a revenue forecast, and the price trend is a cited trend, labeled as one. Open questions are stated as propositions with protocols. The engineering and the measured results are in the research paper.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2" id="companion">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Companion paper</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">The engineering, theory and measured results are in <a href="/papers/rce/" class="text-brand-cyan">The Reality Code Engine: One Form, Many Fits, and the Low-Entropy Path to Autonomous Coding</a> (<a href="/about/rce/" class="text-brand-cyan">about</a>).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/rce-economics/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read paper → /papers/rce-economics/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/rce-economics.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/figures/rce/intent-entropy.svg" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/30 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Figure: intent and entropy
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
